message.content:
{
  "window_id": "w0013",
  "observed_failures": [
    {
      "id": "F1_null_written_as_empty_string",
      "filename": "078.jpg",
      "symptom": "total_amount cell written as empty string '' instead of a real null; feedback marks amount incorrect",
      "evidence": "predictions row for 078.jpg has total_amount == '' (not None); candidate xlsx skill explicitly forbids '' / 'None' / 'NaN' but source run did not follow it"
    },
    {
      "id": "F2_total_picked_from_corrupted_rounded_line",
      "filename": "074.jpg",
      "symptom": "predicted 702.00; image clearly shows Subtotal/Total incl. of GST/Payment all 102.00 and 'Total Amt Rounded' = 102.00",
      "evidence": "LLM trace shows OCR produced 'Total Amt Rounded ——S«702.00' (OCR noise fused with the number). Extractor still returned the LAST TOTAL-matching candidate, so a clearly corrupted trailing line overrode three internally consistent 102.00 lines above it"
    },
    {
      "id": "F3_wrong_total_tier_picked",
      "filename": "077.jpg",
      "symptom": "predicted 23.26 (= 'Total (Inclusive of GST)') instead of the final standalone 'TOTAL: 23.25' (after Rounding Adj -0.01)",
      "evidence": "image shows both 'Total (Inclusive of GST): 23.26' and a bold 'TOTAL: 23.25' as the final payable line; extractor treated both as generic TOTAL hits and failed to prefer the final standalone TOTAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "F4_date_digit_confusion",
      "filename": "034.jpg",
      "symptom": "predicted 2018-08-09; image date reads 09/03/2018 (i.e. 2018-03-09)",
      "evidence": "LLM trace confirms OCR returned '09/08/2018' with default PSM and '09/03/2018' with preprocessed PSM-6; first-match date policy locked in the first OCR variant without cross-checking"
    },
    {
      "id": "F5_iteration_limit_without_natural_completion",
      "filename": "<run-level>",
      "symptom": "termination_reason = max_iterations after 65 iterations; agent never invoked any skill via invoke_skill (n_skill_invocations=0) despite skills being preloaded",
      "evidence": "execution_metadata.termination_reason, agent_iterations=65, response_tool_call_counts shows terminal/think/file_editor but no invoke_skill; agent re-derived logic in-place instead of following skill checklists"
    }
  ],
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "id": "RC1_total_priority_missing_final_standalone_total",
      "description": "Priority tiers collapse 'Total (Inclusive of GST)', 'Net Total', 'Total Amt Rounded', and a final bold 'TOTAL:' into one generic \\\\bTOTAL\\\\b tier. On receipts with a Rounding Adj line, the oracle tracks the post-rounding standalone TOTAL, which must outrank any earlier 'Total (incl. of GST)' line.",
      "related_failures": ["F3_wrong_total_tier_picked"]
    },
    {
      "id": "RC2_no_consistency_check_on_candidate_number",
      "description": "When several lines mention TOTAL, the extractor picks the last keyword hit regardless of whether its number is corroborated anywhere else in the receipt. OCR corruption on one isolated line (e.g. '——S«702.00') therefore wins over three agreeing 102.00 lines.",
      "related_failures": ["F2_total_picked_from_corrupted_rounded_line"]
    },
    {
      "id": "RC3_null_contract_not_enforced_at_write_time",
      "description": "Extraction correctly returns None on failure, but the Excel writer path did not coerce None to an empty/real-null cell; a '' sneaks through. The xlsx skill's strict-schema checklist says 'write None not \"\"' but has no copy-paste writer that guarantees it, and no self-check that re-reads the file and asserts non-null cells are real strings.",
      "related_failures": ["F1_null_written_as_empty_string"]
    },
    {
      "id": "RC4_single_ocr_pass_commits_too_early_on_dates",
      "description": "Date extraction stops on the first regex hit from the first OCR variant. For receipts with glyph ambiguity (3/8, 0/O, 1/l), different PSMs produce different digits; without cross-variant voting or anchor-word scoping ('Date :'), the first noisy answer wins.",
      "related_failures": ["F4_date_digit_confusion"]
    },
    {
      "id": "RC5_skills_not_actually_invoked",
      "description": "Skills live only as preloaded markdown; the agent is not routed through them for receipt tasks. With 65 iterations consumed on ad-hoc regex tuning in extract.py, the batch terminated at max_iterations instead of a natural stop, meaning any late-stage refinement (null-writing, voting) never executed.",
      "related_failures": ["F5_iteration_limit_without_natural_completion"]
    }
  ],
  "skill_defects": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defects": [
        "TOTAL_PRIORITY lacks a dedicated tier for a final standalone 'TOTAL:' line that appears below a 'Rounding Adj' / 'Total Rounded' / 'Total After Adj' row; 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' is treated as equally specific.",
        "No rule to deprioritize candidate lines whose OCR text around the number contains obvious noise (long runs of dashes/underscores, non-ASCII punctuation fused to digits) — exactly the '——S«702.00' pattern.",
        "No cross-line corroboration: when the same amount appears on Subtotal/Payment/Total-incl-GST, that amount should be preferred over an isolated keyword hit.",
        "Multi-pass OCR described but not required; the pipeline is still single-pass. No voting/agreement logic across PSM variants for either date or total.",
        "Date extraction returns the first regex match in reading order with no preference for a line that actually starts with a 'Date' / 'Tarikh' / 'Invoice Date' anchor, so random ID numbers or OCR-garbled dates can win."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defects": [
        "Strict-schema section warns against '' / 'None' / 'NaN' but does not supply a mandatory 'write and verify' helper that converts any falsy-but-not-None value (including '') to None before to_excel.",
        "The post-write verification snippet checks shape and dtype but does not assert that total_amount cells are either None or a str matching ^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$; a stray '' would pass the current checks.",
        "No explicit statement that pandas NaN must be replaced with None via df.where(pd.notna(df), None) or astype(object).where(...) before writing to openpyxl, which is the common path through which '' and NaN leak in."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "openai-vision",
      "defects": [
        "Not referenced from image-ocr as a disagreement-breaker for low-confidence Tesseract outputs (e.g. date digit confusion, or when two PSM variants disagree on the total). A brief cross-reference would let the ocr pipeline escalate ambiguous fields rather than guessing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "pdf",
      "defects": [
        "No defects relevant to this JPG receipt task; skill is out of scope but still loaded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill": "video-frame-extraction",
      "defects": [
        "No defects relevant to this JPG receipt task; skill is out of scope but still loaded."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "repair_recommendations": [
    {
      "target": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a highest-priority tier for the final rounded/standalone TOTAL. Insert regexes like r'^\\s*TOTAL\\s*[:\\-]?\\s*$' (label-only line, number on next line), r'\\bTOTAL\\s+ROUNDED\\b', r'\\bTOTAL\\s+AFTER\\s+(ADJ|ROUNDING)\\b', r'\\bROUNDED\\s+TOTAL\\b', and r'\\bTOTAL\\s+AMT\\s+ROUNDED\\b' ABOVE the generic \\bTOTAL\\b / \\bAMOUNT\\b tier, but BELOW GRAND TOTAL. Document that when a 'Rounding Adj' line is present anywhere in the receipt, these post-rounding labels must beat 'Total (Inclusive of GST)'.",
      "rationale": "Fixes F3 (077.jpg 23.25 vs 23.26) and generalizes to any receipt with a 'Rounding Adj' line; keeps existing exclusion list intact."
    },
    {
      "target": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add an OCR-noise penalty to candidate selection. When collecting candidates in a tier, score each by (a) presence of >=2 consecutive non-alphanumeric glyphs (—, ~, «, S« etc.) adjacent to the number, and (b) whether the parsed amount also appears on at least one other non-excluded line (Subtotal, Payment, Cash, Total incl. GST). Prefer the highest-scoring candidate; break ties by last-occurrence. Keep the two-line fallback only for clean lines.",
      "rationale": "Fixes F2 (074.jpg 102.00 vs 702.00): 102.00 appears on 4 lines, 702.00 only on the OCR-corrupted 'Total Amt Rounded ——S«702.00' line."
    },
    {
      "target": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Make multi-pass OCR mandatory and add a voting step. Run at least {default PSM, PSM 6 on autocontrast grayscale}; run extract_total/extract_date on each; if both return values, prefer the value that (a) is produced by the higher-priority tier, then (b) agrees across passes, then (c) comes from the pass whose text contains more dictionary words / fewer non-ASCII glyphs. Document this as the default pipeline, not a fallback.",
      "rationale": "Fixes F4 (034.jpg 09/03 vs 09/08) and hardens against single-PSM failures without over-indexing to one receipt."
    },
    {
      "target": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Scope date extraction to a 'date-anchor' window first. Prefer regex matches on lines containing any of ('Date', 'Tarikh', 'Invoice Date', 'Receipt Date', 'Order Date'); only fall back to free-text scan if no anchored match parses. Also reject years outside a plausible window (e.g. 2010–2030) before accepting.",
      "rationale": "Reduces misreads on invoice IDs and bogus years and makes multi-pass voting meaningful."
    },
    {
      "target": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add a required 'write_strict_schema' recipe: (1) build DataFrame with explicit columns and dtype=object; (2) df = df.where(pd.notna(df), None); (3) df.replace({'': None, 'None': None, 'nan': None, 'NaN': None}, inplace=True); (4) write with to_excel(sheet_name=..., index=False); (5) re-open with openpyxl and assert every data cell is either None or matches the task's regex (for monetary: ^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$). Make the re-read assertion part of the checklist, not optional.",
      "rationale": "Fixes F1 (078.jpg '') and blocks the entire class of 'empty string instead of null' failures across any future strict-schema task."
    },
    {
      "target": "xlsx",
      "change": "In the Pitfalls list, add a bullet: 'Any extractor that returns Optional[str] must have its '' outputs normalized to None before DataFrame construction; the writer must not accept '' as a valid monetary cell.' Cross-reference this from image-ocr's Structured Field Extraction section.",
      "rationale": "Keeps the null contract visible at both producer (image-ocr) and consumer (xlsx) sides."
    },
    {
      "target": "image-ocr",
      "change": "In the per-image pipeline example, change the return contract so that process_receipt NEVER returns the literal string '' for a failed field — only None. Add a self-check bullet: 'If total_str is set, it matches ^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$; else it is None.'",
      "rationale": "Makes the null contract enforced at the extraction boundary, not only at the Excel boundary."
    },
    {
      "target": "openai-vision",
      "change": "Add a short 'Tie-breaking for Tesseract' section describing how to invoke a single high-detail GPT-4o call on a cropped receipt region when image-ocr's multi-pass voting still disagrees on a date digit or an amount. Keep it opt-in and cost-bounded (1 call per ambiguous field, not per image).",
      "rationale": "Gives image-ocr a documented escalation path without forcing vision calls on every receipt."
    },
    {
      "target": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a top-of-file 'When invoked by the agent' note telling the agent to use invoke_skill('image-ocr') and follow the pipeline rather than re-implementing regexes inline. Mirror the same note in xlsx.",
      "rationale": "Addresses F5: skills were preloaded but never invoked; the agent spent 65 iterations hand-rolling the same patterns and hit the iteration limit."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.78
}
